# Timing-independent firmware/ corpus for the P3.4 lockstep harness --
# per the plan, the subset of firmware/Makefile targets whose outcome
# doesn't depend on interrupt/JTAG/debugger timing (excludes
# interrupt_test, uart_plic_meip_test, uart_plic_seip_test,
# m10_debug_test). One `make -C firmware` TARGET name per line (not a
# path -- run_lockstep.sh builds each before running it).
#
# These programs halt via a trailing ebreak (crt0.s's own convention,
# checked externally by each program's own dedicated _tb.sv in the
# regular regression suite) rather than writing a tohost location, so
# they're unusable with lockstep_tb.sv's +TOHOST_ADDR completion path --
# run_lockstep.sh instead runs each with +MAX_RETIRE=<bound> (comparing
# every retirement up to that bound, including the harmless repeated
# retirements of the post-ebreak halt loop). #-comments and blank lines
# ignored.
#
# target | hex file (relative to firmware/) | MAX_RETIRE bound
#
# `all` (crt0.hex, hello.c) was previously excluded here: lockstep_mem.sv's
# response mux re-derived its RAM/MMIO decode live from the arbiter's
# downstream address, which raced with ref_core.sv's own wb_mem_addr_o/
# cyc_o combinationally reverting to 0 on ack, forming a zero-delay
# simulation loop on hello.c's first UART write. Fixed by latching the
# decode (target_q) instead, mirroring wb_addr_decoder.sv's own pattern.
# Re-enabled below.
all|crt0.hex|2000
csr_test|csr_test.hex|3000
m_test|m_test.hex|3000
priv_test|priv_test.hex|4000
a_test|a_test.hex|3000
c_test|c_test.hex|3000
sv39_real_test|sv39_real_test.hex|6000
